WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.240
to pay for the sin of humanity.

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:03.839
I'm thankful that he was buried,

00:00:03.839 --> 00:00:07.239
but he rose conquering sin, death, and the grave.

00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:09.520
He is alive forevermore.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.640
And as they said, shout and proclaim

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.479
that he's coming back, amen.

00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:14.859
And if you're saved this morning,

00:00:14.859 --> 00:00:17.559
you've trusted Jesus Christ as your personal savior.

00:00:17.559 --> 00:00:18.879
He's coming back for you.

00:00:18.879 --> 00:00:21.959
Listen for the trumpet, Jesus is coming, amen.

00:00:21.959 --> 00:00:24.239
And we are thankful and we are blessed.

00:00:24.239 --> 00:00:26.239
Thank you for singing this morning.

00:00:26.239 --> 00:00:27.819
And I've already sensed

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:29.879
that we're worshiping the Lord today, amen.

00:00:29.879 --> 00:00:32.259
He is worthy of our worship.

00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:34.380
Luke 19 in your Bibles this morning,

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.099
Luke chapter number 19,

00:00:36.099 --> 00:00:38.619
and I'm gonna read the first 10 verses of Scripture

00:00:38.619 --> 00:00:40.099
as we get into the message this morning.

00:00:40.099 --> 00:00:42.419
It's a familiar passage of Scripture.

00:00:42.419 --> 00:00:46.220
And I hope that this morning the Lord will help us

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.180
as we look at this portion of Scripture,

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.459
encourage us and challenge us to be doers of the word

00:00:52.459 --> 00:00:54.540
and not hearers only.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.180
In Luke 19 in verse number one,

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.020
the Bible says,

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:02.560
and Jesus entered and passed through Jericho.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.040
Behold, there was a man named Zacchaeus,

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:10.839
which was the chief among the publicans and he was rich.

00:01:10.839 --> 00:01:14.720
And he sought to see Jesus who he was

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.680
and could not for the press

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:20.239
because he was little of stature.

00:01:20.239 --> 00:01:23.559
And he ran before and climbed up into a sycamore tree

00:01:23.559 --> 00:01:27.699
to see him for he was to pass that way.

00:01:27.699 --> 00:01:29.419
And when Jesus came to the place,

00:01:29.419 --> 00:01:32.139
he looked up and saw him and said unto him,

00:01:32.139 --> 00:01:36.220
Zacchaeus, make haste and come down

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:39.379
for today I must abide at thy house.

00:01:39.379 --> 00:01:43.419
And he made haste and came down and received him joyfully.

00:01:43.419 --> 00:01:44.260
When they saw it,

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:47.059
they all murmured saying that he was gone

00:01:47.059 --> 00:01:49.980
to be guest with a man that is a sinner.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:52.500
And Zacchaeus stood and said unto the Lord,

00:01:52.519 --> 00:01:57.000
behold, Lord, the half of my goods I give to the poor.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.000
And if I've taken anything from any man

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.279
by false accusation, I restore him fourfold.

00:02:02.279 --> 00:02:04.599
And Jesus said unto him, notice in verse nine,

00:02:04.599 --> 00:02:09.479
this day is salvation come to this house

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:12.380
for as much as he also is a son of Abraham,

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:15.679
for the son of man has come to seek and to save

00:02:15.679 --> 00:02:18.479
that which was lost.

00:02:18.479 --> 00:02:20.000
As we look at this portion of scripture,

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.199
I've titled the message from verse number nine,

00:02:22.199 --> 00:02:26.699
this day is salvation come to this house.

00:02:26.699 --> 00:02:28.460
As we get to look at this portion of scripture,

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:31.740
I'm reminded that tomorrow personally will be 29 years

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:35.380
since I trusted Jesus Christ as my personal savior.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.660
And I'm so thankful that on that particular day

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:40.179
that the Holy Spirit of God convinced me

00:02:40.179 --> 00:02:41.740
of my need for the Savior,

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:44.059
the only Savior, the Lord Jesus Christ.

00:02:44.059 --> 00:02:47.660
And it was not much to convince me that I was guilty,

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.220
that I was a sinner.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.820
The problem was that I didn't know

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:54.020
what was going to happen when I died as a sinner.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.559
I had this idea that I could be a good enough person

00:02:56.559 --> 00:02:59.500
and maybe at the end of the whole situation,

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.179
there'd be this giant scale and it would determine

00:03:02.179 --> 00:03:05.460
whether I'd have entrance to or not to heaven.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.300
If someone were to ask me, if you were to die today,

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.820
are you sure that heaven is your home?

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:14.080
My answer at that point would have been, I hope so.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.279
And I had zero assurance, it was just simply a hope,

00:03:18.279 --> 00:03:22.279
a wishful thinking that that would be the case.

00:03:22.279 --> 00:03:25.039
However, 29 years ago tomorrow,

00:03:25.039 --> 00:03:27.679
I got on my knees in the living room of our house

00:03:27.679 --> 00:03:29.240
in Southern California,

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.080
and I recognized that I was a sinner

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:32.880
and Jesus was the only Savior.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.440
And I prayed and asked him to be my personal Savior.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.320
And on that day, he saved me.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.679
And what a joy and what a blessing.

00:03:40.679 --> 00:03:42.320
And from that day to this day,

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.399
if someone were to ask me,

00:03:43.399 --> 00:03:45.600
are you sure that heaven is your home?

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.960
I could answer, absolutely,

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:50.559
with 100% confidence and assurance

00:03:50.559 --> 00:03:53.119
because it's not based upon what I did,

00:03:53.119 --> 00:03:55.360
but it's based upon what Jesus Christ did

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.000
on the cross of Calvary,

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.520
his death, burial, and glorious resurrection.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.240
And I would say it this way,

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.039
just as we've seen in Luke chapter 19,

00:04:05.039 --> 00:04:10.039
it was a personal decision on a particular day.

00:04:10.279 --> 00:04:13.759
The decision was mine personally, it was not my dad's.

00:04:13.759 --> 00:04:15.360
He was there in the room with me,

00:04:16.119 --> 00:04:18.559
but it wasn't his decision, it was my decision.

00:04:18.559 --> 00:04:20.760
And it was on a particular day.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.040
Jesus said to Nicodemus in John chapter number three,

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:29.000
marvel not that I say unto thee, ye must be born again.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.760
And on that day, I'm so thankful that I was born again.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:34.760
I was saved by the grace of God.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:37.399
As we look at this familiar portion of scripture

00:04:37.399 --> 00:04:38.760
in Luke chapter 19,

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:42.359
we see this interaction between the Lord Jesus Christ

00:04:42.359 --> 00:04:43.679
and Zacchaeus.

00:04:43.679 --> 00:04:46.160
I said that it was a familiar passage of scripture

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:47.920
for many of us,

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.799
and you've heard perhaps this portion of scripture

00:04:50.799 --> 00:04:51.799
at some point.

00:04:51.799 --> 00:04:54.160
Verse number 10 is an oft quoted verse

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.600
that reveals to us and reminds us

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.959
of the singular purpose

00:04:57.959 --> 00:05:00.079
of the coming of the Lord Jesus Christ.

00:05:00.079 --> 00:05:04.160
And that is to seek and to save that which was lost.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:07.799
And I'm so thankful that he is a seeking savior.

00:05:07.799 --> 00:05:09.399
And we find here this morning

00:05:09.399 --> 00:05:12.519
that oftentimes even in Sunday school classes

00:05:12.519 --> 00:05:14.200
or in junior church classes

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.000
or vacation Bible schools

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.760
that we'll sing that song

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.200
about Zacchaeus was a wee little man

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.720
and a wee little man was he.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.079
And some of you know that song

00:05:23.079 --> 00:05:25.279
and I'm not gonna sing it for you this morning.

00:05:25.279 --> 00:05:26.920
We've already had some great music

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.519
and I don't wanna spoil that.

00:05:28.519 --> 00:05:31.119
But the reality is that we might be familiar

00:05:31.119 --> 00:05:34.160
because of knowing some of those things.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.480
But as we dig in here to this portion of scripture,

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.880
I want you to consider three things as we look here.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.399
Number one, if you're taking notes,

00:05:43.239 --> 00:05:46.160
I want you to notice the condition of Zacchaeus.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.760
The condition of Zacchaeus.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.519
We see that he's an individual

00:05:49.519 --> 00:05:50.859
and we find that as you study

00:05:50.859 --> 00:05:52.239
through this portion of scripture

00:05:52.239 --> 00:05:53.980
that the Bible tells us

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.920
that there were a great number of people.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.600
He says in verse number three,

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.320
he could not for the press

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:01.799
because he was little of stature.

00:06:01.799 --> 00:06:05.040
And so therefore he climbed up into that sycamore tree.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:06.679
There's a number of people there,

00:06:06.679 --> 00:06:08.920
but it's always amazing to me

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:10.399
that as you study the scriptures

00:06:10.399 --> 00:06:12.480
and especially in the gospel records,

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:15.600
the interactions of the Lord Jesus Christ,

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:19.279
you find that though there's multitudes of people,

00:06:19.279 --> 00:06:24.200
oftentimes the focus of scripture is on an individual.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:28.320
There were multitudes, but there's a certain leper.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.179
There's a press of people,

00:06:30.179 --> 00:06:33.839
but Zacchaeus is the one that zeroed in on here.

00:06:33.839 --> 00:06:36.559
We find that as you look at Mark chapter number two,

00:06:36.559 --> 00:06:38.079
that there's so many people

00:06:38.079 --> 00:06:41.640
that they can't even get the man into the door,

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:43.559
into the presence of Jesus.

00:06:43.559 --> 00:06:45.399
But yet the Bible tells us

00:06:45.399 --> 00:06:48.519
that they let him down through a roof tile

00:06:48.519 --> 00:06:50.480
and that man that was born of four.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:54.880
And over and over you find that we serve a God

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:58.839
who is a God who loves the entire world,

00:06:58.839 --> 00:07:01.839
but he's interested in the individuals.

00:07:01.839 --> 00:07:05.079
I'm so thankful that the Bible teaches us

00:07:05.079 --> 00:07:07.239
that God so loved the world.

00:07:07.239 --> 00:07:08.640
I'm thankful for that,

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:11.160
but I'm reminded like what the songwriters said,

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.519
wonderful things in the Bible I see,

00:07:13.519 --> 00:07:18.519
but this is the dearest that Jesus loves me.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:22.160
Praise the Lord that he is a personal God

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.440
and he's a personal savior.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:26.359
And we see the condition of this man, Zacchaeus.

00:07:26.359 --> 00:07:28.640
Notice with me in verse number two,

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:30.679
we find the condition of this man

00:07:30.679 --> 00:07:33.660
and we first think about and notice his position.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:34.959
The Bible says in verse number two,

00:07:34.959 --> 00:07:37.760
and behold, there was a man named Zacchaeus.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:39.000
Notice what the Bible says,

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:43.359
which was the chief among the publicans.

00:07:43.359 --> 00:07:46.440
And so it's a noticed with regard

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.619
to the position of this man

00:07:48.619 --> 00:07:50.760
that he's the chief among the publicans.

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:53.260
It doesn't just tell us that he was a publican,

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:55.679
but he's chief among the publicans.

00:07:55.679 --> 00:07:58.519
Can I tell you this morning that there are some in life

00:07:58.519 --> 00:08:00.440
that are concerned primarily

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:03.260
with what their position in life is.

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:08.059
They are always seeking after a title and a position

00:08:08.059 --> 00:08:11.380
and that's what they find some level of satisfaction

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:16.019
and some level of contentment in is that position.

00:08:16.019 --> 00:08:19.540
And we find here as we look at Luke chapter 19,

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:23.179
that this man Zacchaeus had position.

00:08:23.179 --> 00:08:26.220
He was chief among the publicans.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:28.260
Not only did he have position,

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:30.500
but we see that he had possessions.

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:32.500
The end of the verse in verse number two says,

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:35.659
and he was rich.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:37.700
He was rich.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:38.739
You know, there's a lot of people

00:08:38.739 --> 00:08:43.659
that are seeking possessions, wealth and rich and riches.

00:08:43.659 --> 00:08:45.099
How much can I get?

00:08:45.099 --> 00:08:47.539
How much can I obtain?

00:08:47.539 --> 00:08:51.140
And we find that many have position

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:53.340
and many have possessions.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:57.140
And this man Zacchaeus, as you study Luke chapter 19

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:59.619
and you consider the condition of this man,

00:08:59.619 --> 00:09:03.500
it seems like from the outside, if you will,

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:04.859
that he's got everything

00:09:04.859 --> 00:09:07.299
that an individual could possibly want.

00:09:07.299 --> 00:09:09.260
I mean, he's got the position.

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:11.340
He has the possessions.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:14.640
And yet we find that this man,

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:17.059
though he was chief among the publicans,

00:09:17.059 --> 00:09:18.599
though he was rich,

00:09:18.599 --> 00:09:21.440
I would submit to you this morning that he was empty.

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:23.859
He was empty.

00:09:23.859 --> 00:09:26.299
Can I tell you this morning that you and I

00:09:26.299 --> 00:09:30.340
have been created by the omnipotent, omniscient God

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:32.780
who loves us and he created us

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:37.340
to have this hole in our souls and our lives

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:40.299
filled only by him.

00:09:40.299 --> 00:09:41.780
There is no position,

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:45.840
there is no possession that can bring you satisfaction

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:48.780
like the Lord Jesus Christ can bring

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:50.820
in the life of an individual.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:55.659
There is a God-shaped hole in every single person

00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:57.539
that's ever been created

00:09:57.539 --> 00:10:00.260
and man tries to fill it with possession.

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:05.260
position and possession, but they find themselves lacking.

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:07.520
They find themselves empty.

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:10.640
Look at it, the Bible says that he sought

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:13.640
to see Jesus, who he was.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:15.980
See this man who, from the outward,

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:18.200
from maybe the friends and those

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.740
that he would rub shoulders with,

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.740
that seemed like he had it all together.

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:24.540
He had the position, he had the possessions,

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:27.240
but yet the Bible says that he sought.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:28.460
See he was seeking.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:30.320
Why, because he wasn't filled.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:31.820
He wasn't satisfied.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:33.860
There was something lacking.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:37.000
And I would submit to you that you could read accounts

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:40.500
of individuals that have written their own testimonies

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:43.380
at the end of life, and they've been asked questions

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:45.340
and interviewed about various things,

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:48.000
and they say this, that I'll tell you one thing,

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.060
that riches, they just don't satisfy.

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:54.940
I'll tell you this, the position, it just doesn't satisfy.

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:56.540
It's temporary.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:58.140
It's temporary.

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:02.300
I was reminded even the other day on Thursday,

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.940
I believe it was, where the Bible tells us

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.180
in the book of Proverbs that riches make wings

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:10.100
and they fly away, and Brianna had asked

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.820
for a little cash for something,

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:14.760
and I went to stick it under her door at the house,

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:16.500
but the air conditioning was on,

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.480
and as soon as I stuck it under the door,

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:20.740
that money went flying out of the door.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.260
And I thought it was kind of comical,

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:24.780
but it reminded me, Holly was standing right next to me,

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.600
and I said, well, like Proverbs said,

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:29.880
riches make wings and they fly away, you know?

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:33.000
But the reality is that those things are temporary.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.600
They're just temporary.

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:37.560
And this man, he was empty.

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:39.700
There was something missing.

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:43.320
Though at the end of the day, he could go home,

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:47.760
or if we could think about it in today's kind of economy

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:51.520
and in our culture, he could walk into the corner office,

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:54.080
so to speak, with the name plaque on the door,

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:57.080
and really, man, he's chief among the publicans,

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:59.660
and he can walk in and he has that position,

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:01.760
and he could buy what he wanted.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:05.040
He had the riches, but he's lacking.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.180
Something was missing.

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:09.880
We find that in verse number eight of our,

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:13.380
or sorry, verse number seven of our text of Scripture,

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:16.360
when we consider the condition of this man, Zacchaeus,

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:18.400
notice what the Bible says in verse number seven.

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:19.920
It says, and when they saw it,

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:23.120
now, to understand the context of what's going on,

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:25.520
remember, there was a great host of people,

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:27.040
as we read in verse number three,

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:29.320
that he could not get to where Jesus was

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:30.420
because of the press,

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:33.440
because of the group of people that were there.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.660
The Bible says that when they saw it,

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:39.360
those that were gathered, they all murmured.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.280
And notice what they said.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:44.840
They said that he, that would be Jesus,

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:49.840
was gone to be guest with a man that is a sinner.

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:53.880
The condition of this man is clearly given to us

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:57.320
in verse number seven, that this man was a sinner.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.800
But can I tell you that that's a universal condition

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.400
of all humanity?

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:03.800
The Bible tells us in Romans chapter number three,

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:07.980
that all have sinned and come short of the glory of God.

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:10.680
The Bible tells us that we are all sinners,

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:12.720
and we understand that there is a problem.

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:15.180
Again, it's a universal condition.

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:17.880
The only individual that's ever walked

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:19.760
upon the face of the earth without sin

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:22.920
is the Lord Jesus Christ, God in flesh.

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:27.440
And he died for us, he who knew no sin,

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:31.400
he took our place, but we understand that this man,

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:34.040
and the statement is so interesting,

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.780
that these that were gathered,

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:38.480
that they would say of this man, Zacchaeus,

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:40.240
he's a sinner.

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:41.320
Guess what?

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:43.640
They were sinners, right?

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:45.840
They're looking at this man and looking at his condition

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:48.280
and saying, oh, he's a sinner.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:49.540
We're all sinners.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:52.000
We're all sinners.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.240
Here's the question is whether we're a sinner

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:57.880
that's been saved by the grace of God, amen?

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:00.800
And the moment I got saved, I didn't stop sinning.

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.080
I should sin less and less as I walk

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:04.760
with the Lord Jesus Christ,

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:07.200
but this flesh was not eradicated,

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.120
and your flesh was not eradicated

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.880
at the moment that you trusted Jesus Christ

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:13.440
as your personal savior.

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:16.559
And we find that those that were throwing

00:14:16.559 --> 00:14:19.080
this statement of he is a sinner,

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:22.580
I can't believe that Jesus went to be guest

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:24.559
with a man that's a sinner.

00:14:24.559 --> 00:14:27.320
They themselves are sinners.

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:30.960
So we understand this morning the condition of Zacchaeus.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:34.200
This morning, I believe that each of us can relate

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:35.880
to the condition of Zacchaeus,

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:38.640
and we can understand in the world in which we live in,

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:43.640
and we can find that whether we had possession or position,

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:46.360
whether those things were true,

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:48.440
we would find that before we were saved,

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:51.440
that there was this thing that something was missing.

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.440
There was some emptiness.

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:56.040
It was a recognition that we're sinners.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.559
This morning, I'm thankful to be saved,

00:14:58.559 --> 00:15:01.540
and I've been saved from the penalty of sin,

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:04.880
but we understand the condition and we can relate.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:06.000
As we look at the text,

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.420
we not only notice the condition of Zacchaeus,

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:09.520
but I want you to notice number two,

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:11.680
the compassion of Jesus.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.660
I'm so thankful this morning that we have a savior

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:15.080
that is compassionate.

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:17.680
I'm so thankful this morning that we have a savior

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:20.080
that is moved with compassion.

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:23.080
And as we look at the passage here that is before us,

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:26.400
we find it quite interesting that in verse number one,

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:29.920
you notice some purpose with regard to the movement

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:31.440
of the Lord Jesus Christ.

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:33.920
It says in Luke 19 in verse number one,

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:38.920
and Jesus entered and passed through Jericho.

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:42.320
It reminds me of what we read in John chapter number four,

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:44.440
when the Bible says that Jesus said

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:47.000
that he must needs go through Samaria.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.760
And we understand that Jericho is a different region

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:53.200
than Samaria, but understand that here in Jericho

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:55.460
is the Bible tells us in verse number one,

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:57.680
that Jesus not only entered into,

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.559
but it said that he passed through Jericho.

00:16:01.559 --> 00:16:06.559
Everything that our Lord does is on purpose and with purpose.

00:16:06.559 --> 00:16:09.240
As we begin reading in verse number one,

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:11.119
and you get down to verse number three,

00:16:11.119 --> 00:16:14.320
and you begin to see about Zacchaeus, how he was seeking,

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:17.880
I would say to you that Jesus was seeking Zacchaeus

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:21.119
long before Zacchaeus was seeking Jesus.

00:16:21.119 --> 00:16:24.640
And I'm so thankful for the way in which Zacchaeus,

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:25.839
how did he know?

00:16:25.839 --> 00:16:28.580
How did he hear about Jesus?

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:31.779
The fame was going abroad of the work

00:16:31.779 --> 00:16:33.520
of the Lord Jesus Christ.

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:37.000
And this man Zacchaeus heard and he's coming,

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:41.760
but understand that Jesus had this divine appointment.

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:44.600
And he specifically, and on purpose,

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:48.119
he entered and he passed through Jericho.

00:16:48.119 --> 00:16:50.380
We find that as you would begin to understand

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:53.920
the compassion of Jesus and recognize the purpose,

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:56.820
but we also see the fact that he's personal.

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:58.839
I mentioned this already a moment ago,

00:16:58.839 --> 00:17:01.320
but I want you to specifically look at verse number five

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:05.640
with me, and the Bible says this in verse number five,

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:10.080
and when Jesus came, notice what it says to the place.

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:12.700
Now think about it again, if I could help us

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:17.080
have this sanctified imagination to see what's taking place,

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:19.360
there's a multitude of people.

00:17:20.279 --> 00:17:22.240
And Jesus is passing through,

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:24.040
you've been in a crowd of people before

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:27.680
and you understand the masses and just kind of passing

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:32.059
and we find that this man Zacchaeus, he's up in a tree.

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:36.800
And he's there because he's desiring to see

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:38.180
the Lord Jesus Christ.

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:39.540
And it tells us that in verse number four,

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:42.580
that he ran before, and so there's so many people,

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:45.100
they're pressed, he couldn't get to where Jesus was,

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:48.140
so he ran ahead, he gets up into this tree

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:52.180
so that he could see the Lord as he passed by.

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:54.460
Now think about that with me.

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:57.020
His longing and desire was to see,

00:17:57.020 --> 00:17:58.140
according to verse number three,

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:02.660
he sought to see Jesus, who he was.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.180
And we find that in verse number four,

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:07.500
that Jesus was to pass that way and he's up in a tree

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:09.220
and having this interest.

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:11.580
Now recognize with me this morning

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:14.100
that he would not know who he was

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:16.200
by simply seeing him pass by.

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:20.940
But it says in verse number five,

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:24.260
that when Jesus came to the place,

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:30.460
he looked up and he saw him and said unto him.

00:18:30.619 --> 00:18:33.059
Now again, there's a lot of people there,

00:18:33.059 --> 00:18:37.020
but Jesus personally starts dealing with Zacchaeus.

00:18:37.020 --> 00:18:39.380
The Bible says this, Zacchaeus,

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:41.700
this is what Jesus says to Zacchaeus,

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:45.299
make haste and come down.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:51.100
For today, do you notice that word, I must?

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:55.260
I must abide at thy house.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:56.739
Isn't that awesome?

00:18:56.739 --> 00:18:58.859
I mean, to think about the compassion

00:18:58.859 --> 00:19:01.140
of the Lord Jesus Christ that he looked at,

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:03.619
saw, and then spoke to Zacchaeus,

00:19:03.619 --> 00:19:06.739
and he told Zacchaeus that to make haste,

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:09.859
I mean, do not delay, there was urgency,

00:19:09.859 --> 00:19:14.859
make haste, come down, for today I must abide at thy house.

00:19:16.619 --> 00:19:19.440
And I'm so thankful for the response in verse number six

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:22.140
that Zacchaeus didn't say, I'm too busy,

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:23.700
maybe some other time.

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:27.979
I'm just, no, he made haste and he came down, amen?

00:19:27.979 --> 00:19:29.460
And praise the Lord for that.

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:32.179
I preached last week from Mark chapter number six,

00:19:32.179 --> 00:19:34.460
that he saw them, and I said this

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:35.979
as we looked at the text of scripture,

00:19:35.979 --> 00:19:38.900
that Jesus knew exactly where the disciples were

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:41.380
in the midst of that sea, and it tells us

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:42.540
that he walked on that water

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:44.679
and he would have passed them by.

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:48.660
But John told us that he records for us

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:52.419
that they willingly received him into the ship

00:19:52.419 --> 00:19:54.940
and how that made all the difference.

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:59.340
Zacchaeus responded well to the invitation

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:00.900
that was given in verse seven.

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:04.900
I want you to notice that this really reveals to us

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:08.900
the compassion of Jesus with working with Zacchaeus here

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:12.900
in Luke chapter 19 reveals to us the primary purpose

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:15.900
that is revealed in verse number 10 to the work

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:17.900
and ministry of the Lord Jesus Christ.

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:21.900
For the Son of Man has come to seek and to save

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:25.900
that which was lost.

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:29.900
I'm thankful that He's a seeking Savior.

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:32.900
I'm thankful that on August 31st, 1997

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:35.900
that He found me and He saved me.

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:37.900
And I'm thankful for many of you that have shared

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:39.900
your personal testimony of salvation with me

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:42.900
that you were saved by the grace of God.

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:45.900
This morning, if you're not saved, if you do not have assurance

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:48.900
that heaven is your home, can I tell you that God loves you?

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:52.900
That Jesus died for you, that He was buried and He rose again.

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:54.900
We've been singing about it this morning.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:56.900
We've had the opportunity to look here this morning

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.900
at this portion of scripture to see the compassion

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:01.900
of the Lord Jesus Christ.

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:05.900
Now, understand as Jesus would go and enter

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:08.900
into the home of Zacchaeus, the Bible says

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:12.900
that Zacchaeus received Him joyfully.

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:15.900
And the Bible doesn't give us all of the details

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:18.900
with regard to the interaction that Zacchaeus

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:20.900
had with Jesus in His house.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:23.900
It's not recorded for us, but can I tell you

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:27.900
that Zacchaeus was seeking, according to verse number three,

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:33.900
to see Jesus in the notice who He was.

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:39.900
He wasn't just seeking Jesus to find out what He could do.

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:42.900
Think about that for a moment.

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:44.900
Herod was gonna seek Jesus for a long time,

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:46.900
wanted to see Him, why?

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:49.900
Because he heard about the miracles, what He could do.

00:21:49.900 --> 00:21:51.900
In John chapter number six, Jesus says,

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:55.900
hey, you're not here because you really desire Me,

00:21:55.900 --> 00:21:58.900
you're here because you ate the bread.

00:21:58.900 --> 00:22:00.900
What He could do.

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:02.900
Can I tell you this morning, there's some people

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:04.900
that wanna seek Jesus so that they can find out

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:07.900
what Jesus can do for them or what He can do.

00:22:07.900 --> 00:22:10.900
But the real question is, who is He?

00:22:10.900 --> 00:22:12.900
Who is He?

00:22:12.900 --> 00:22:15.900
See, Zacchaeus wasn't so much interested

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:17.900
in seeing some miracle.

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:20.900
Now, he did see a miracle, we'll see it in just a moment.

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:23.900
But he was interested, who is He?

00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:25.900
It reminds me of what Jesus said

00:22:25.900 --> 00:22:27.900
in Matthew chapter number 16

00:22:27.900 --> 00:22:29.900
when He's speaking to His disciples.

00:22:29.900 --> 00:22:32.900
Whom do men say that I am?

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:34.900
Who is Jesus?

00:22:34.900 --> 00:22:37.900
And in that day, in the first century,

00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:39.900
there were some that said, well, it's John the Baptist,

00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:43.900
Jeremiah, one of the prophets.

00:22:43.900 --> 00:22:47.900
And then Jesus says, but whom say ye that I am?

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:49.900
And some of you are familiar with the passage

00:22:49.900 --> 00:22:51.900
and Peter stands up and he says,

00:22:51.900 --> 00:22:55.900
thou art the Christ, the Son of the living God.

00:22:55.900 --> 00:22:58.900
Praise God for that proclamation.

00:22:58.900 --> 00:23:01.900
And we find this morning that the question

00:23:01.900 --> 00:23:04.900
still remains in 2026, who is Jesus?

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:06.900
Who is He?

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:08.900
He is God in flesh.

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:09.900
He is the Messiah.

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:11.900
He is the promised one.

00:23:11.900 --> 00:23:13.900
We find that He is the Redeemer,

00:23:13.900 --> 00:23:15.900
the Savior of the world.

00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:17.900
At this point in Luke chapter 19,

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:19.900
He's not yet gone to the cross of Calvary,

00:23:19.900 --> 00:23:21.900
but soon He would.

00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:23.900
And we know that if you read John 17

00:23:23.900 --> 00:23:25.900
that it was so absolutely certain

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:29.900
that Jesus would go and fulfill what He came to do

00:23:29.900 --> 00:23:32.900
that He could speak of the event being finished

00:23:32.900 --> 00:23:36.900
though He had not even gone to the cross yet.

00:23:36.900 --> 00:23:39.900
And we find the compassion

00:23:39.900 --> 00:23:42.900
that Jesus stops at that tree

00:23:42.900 --> 00:23:44.900
and He looks up and He says,

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:46.900
Make haste, come down.

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:51.900
I must abide at thy house today.

00:23:51.900 --> 00:23:54.900
And we begin to look at this portion of Scripture

00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:57.900
and we begin to see this personal interaction

00:23:57.900 --> 00:23:59.900
between the Lord Jesus Christ, God in flesh,

00:23:59.900 --> 00:24:02.900
and Zacchaeus and we rejoice

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:04.900
in understanding at this point

00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:06.900
all that has transpired

00:24:06.900 --> 00:24:08.900
and that Jesus would reveal Himself.

00:24:08.900 --> 00:24:10.900
Listen, I want you to know this morning,

00:24:10.900 --> 00:24:13.900
I've said this to so many people over the years,

00:24:13.900 --> 00:24:17.900
if you want to know truth, God will reveal truth to you.

00:24:17.900 --> 00:24:19.900
He is truth.

00:24:19.900 --> 00:24:22.900
Jesus said, I am the way, the truth, and the life.

00:24:22.900 --> 00:24:26.900
No man cometh unto the Father but by me.

00:24:26.900 --> 00:24:29.900
And we find that the Lord Jesus Christ,

00:24:29.900 --> 00:24:31.900
He's given to us a Bible.

00:24:31.900 --> 00:24:34.900
We have the Scriptures that reveal to us

00:24:34.900 --> 00:24:37.900
who He is and what He has done.

00:24:37.900 --> 00:24:42.900
And we find that He wants people, humanity, to know truth.

00:24:42.900 --> 00:24:45.900
See, because He's compassionate, because He's love,

00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:48.900
we've been dealing with this on Wednesday evenings

00:24:48.900 --> 00:24:50.900
looking through the book of 2 John.

00:24:50.900 --> 00:24:52.900
God is love.

00:24:52.900 --> 00:24:54.900
God is truth.

00:24:54.900 --> 00:24:57.900
Because God is love, God gave us truth.

00:24:57.900 --> 00:25:00.900
Because He loves us, He wants us to know the truth.

00:25:00.900 --> 00:25:03.900
And the truth is that all the way back in the beginning

00:25:03.900 --> 00:25:08.900
that God made humanity.

00:25:08.900 --> 00:25:10.900
And when He made Adam and He made Eve,

00:25:10.900 --> 00:25:12.900
He made them perfect.

00:25:12.900 --> 00:25:16.900
But the truth is that they sinned.

00:25:16.900 --> 00:25:19.900
And when they sinned, the Bible tells us that death

00:25:19.900 --> 00:25:21.900
entered into the world.

00:25:21.900 --> 00:25:24.900
The Bible says that we've all sinned.

00:25:24.900 --> 00:25:26.900
I believe this morning that every single one of us,

00:25:26.900 --> 00:25:29.900
including Zacchaeus, would be able to acknowledge

00:25:29.900 --> 00:25:31.900
that we're sinners.

00:25:31.900 --> 00:25:34.900
And it's all because of what happened all the way back in the garden.

00:25:34.900 --> 00:25:39.900
When Adam and Eve partook of the forbidden fruit,

00:25:39.900 --> 00:25:42.900
and they took part and their eyes were opened.

00:25:42.900 --> 00:25:44.900
And you know what they tried to do?

00:25:44.900 --> 00:25:46.900
They tried to cover their nakedness.

00:25:46.900 --> 00:25:50.900
And they tried to, by the works of their own hands,

00:25:50.900 --> 00:25:54.900
they tried to cover their nakedness.

00:25:54.900 --> 00:25:57.900
Listen, that's what so many people are trying to do today

00:25:57.900 --> 00:25:59.900
with regard to covering their sin.

00:25:59.900 --> 00:26:01.900
They're trying to do good things.

00:26:01.900 --> 00:26:03.900
I don't remember which one sang the part of the song

00:26:03.900 --> 00:26:07.900
this morning from the Trejos, but about their good works.

00:26:07.900 --> 00:26:10.900
