00:40:00.980 --> 00:40:02.780
on a particular day.

00:40:04.740 --> 00:40:08.940
Paul writes about his kinsmen, his brethren,

00:40:08.940 --> 00:40:11.180
according to the flesh, the Jewish people,

00:40:11.180 --> 00:40:14.900
and he writes in Romans 9 and Romans chapter number 10

00:40:14.900 --> 00:40:17.380
that he had great heaviness and continual sorrow

00:40:17.380 --> 00:40:18.860
in his heart for them, why?

00:40:18.860 --> 00:40:21.500
For I could wish that myself were accursed from Christ

00:40:21.500 --> 00:40:23.820
for my brethren, my kinsmen, according to the flesh.

00:40:23.820 --> 00:40:25.980
Brethren, in chapter 10 of the book of Romans,

00:40:25.980 --> 00:40:29.980
he says my heart's desire and prayer to God for Israel

00:40:29.980 --> 00:40:32.780
is that they might be saved,

00:40:32.780 --> 00:40:37.220
but as much as I would want for any person to be saved,

00:40:37.220 --> 00:40:40.460
it's a personal decision on a particular day.

00:40:41.960 --> 00:40:44.340
We have three children, most of you know that.

00:40:45.920 --> 00:40:48.260
We prayed for our children to trust Christ

00:40:48.260 --> 00:40:49.920
as their personal savior,

00:40:50.780 --> 00:40:54.380
and it was a personal decision on a particular day.

00:40:55.260 --> 00:41:00.260
I could not get saved for Julianna, Brianna, or Joseph.

00:41:00.700 --> 00:41:04.380
I could not get saved for them,

00:41:04.380 --> 00:41:07.340
but I could pray that they would get saved,

00:41:07.340 --> 00:41:09.860
and I'm thankful to be able to report this morning

00:41:09.860 --> 00:41:12.260
that all three of our children trust at Christ

00:41:12.260 --> 00:41:13.760
as their personal savior.

00:41:15.260 --> 00:41:19.060
We have, thank God, two grandchildren right now,

00:41:19.060 --> 00:41:22.180
a third one on the way in January,

00:41:22.180 --> 00:41:25.180
and those two grandchildren, Nova and Bellamy,

00:41:25.180 --> 00:41:27.260
you know what I pray, Mark, for them daily,

00:41:27.260 --> 00:41:28.540
that they'd be saved,

00:41:29.580 --> 00:41:31.100
but you know what I can't do for them?

00:41:31.100 --> 00:41:32.860
I can't get saved for them.

00:41:32.860 --> 00:41:35.020
Nova's gonna be three in just a few weeks.

00:41:35.020 --> 00:41:36.540
She doesn't fully understand,

00:41:36.540 --> 00:41:39.580
but she'll say to us often when we're FaceTiming,

00:41:39.580 --> 00:41:40.620
because they live in Hawaii,

00:41:40.620 --> 00:41:43.300
and she was trying to make me cry last night,

00:41:43.300 --> 00:41:45.560
Papa, can you come to my birthday party?

00:41:46.620 --> 00:41:47.860
And I said, honey, I can't.

00:41:47.860 --> 00:41:50.340
She said, Papa, please.

00:41:50.340 --> 00:41:51.640
Man, if you're not a grandfather,

00:41:52.060 --> 00:41:53.920
you don't know what that does to your heart,

00:41:53.920 --> 00:41:54.940
but she lives in Hawaii.

00:41:54.940 --> 00:41:56.520
I can't just jump in a car

00:41:56.520 --> 00:41:58.400
and get over there for her birthday,

00:42:00.400 --> 00:42:03.400
but she says, can you read me a story about God?

00:42:04.800 --> 00:42:07.080
Can you read me a story about Jesus?

00:42:07.960 --> 00:42:09.680
That thrills me,

00:42:09.680 --> 00:42:11.580
but you know, she's gonna come to a point in her life,

00:42:11.580 --> 00:42:13.800
I don't know what the age is gonna be,

00:42:13.800 --> 00:42:16.200
but there needs to be a personal decision

00:42:16.200 --> 00:42:19.720
on a particular day for Nova Kinsley Mann.

00:42:20.720 --> 00:42:23.240
She needs to be saved.

00:42:23.240 --> 00:42:24.800
I can't do it for her.

00:42:26.080 --> 00:42:28.180
So what am I saying this morning?

00:42:28.180 --> 00:42:29.320
Have you been saved?

00:42:30.320 --> 00:42:33.280
Have you trusted Jesus Christ as your personal savior?

00:42:33.280 --> 00:42:35.280
Could you say this morning

00:42:35.280 --> 00:42:39.900
that there was a personal decision on a particular day?

00:42:39.900 --> 00:42:42.520
Someone said it this way, God only has children,

00:42:42.520 --> 00:42:44.280
he has no grandchildren.

00:42:44.280 --> 00:42:45.240
What does he mean by that?

00:42:45.240 --> 00:42:48.960
Well, every single person has to trust Christ personally.

00:42:50.480 --> 00:42:52.120
The Bible says in John chapter one,

00:42:52.120 --> 00:42:55.700
that he came to his own and his own received him not,

00:42:56.720 --> 00:42:58.240
but to as many as received him,

00:42:59.100 --> 00:43:02.240
to them gave he power to become the sons of God,

00:43:02.240 --> 00:43:06.580
even to them that believe on his name.

00:43:06.580 --> 00:43:09.280
Can I tell you this morning that God loves you

00:43:09.280 --> 00:43:13.440
and he died for you and he rose again,

00:43:13.440 --> 00:43:16.080
he conquered sin, death and the grave.

00:43:16.080 --> 00:43:19.240
He paid everything that had to be paid

00:43:19.240 --> 00:43:20.480
so that you could go to heaven.

00:43:20.480 --> 00:43:25.480
He said it this way on the cross, it is finished.

00:43:26.040 --> 00:43:27.960
He didn't say it is started

00:43:27.960 --> 00:43:30.000
and then you go ahead and take it and finish.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:31.760
No, he said it is finished.

00:43:32.720 --> 00:43:37.720
And he offers to us salvation, a free gift, eternal life.

00:43:38.080 --> 00:43:41.240
The question this morning is, have you received it?

00:43:41.240 --> 00:43:42.520
Has there been that day,

00:43:42.520 --> 00:43:46.880
personal decision on a particular day?

00:43:46.880 --> 00:43:49.220
This morning, if you cannot say with certainty

00:43:50.000 --> 00:43:52.540
that I know for sure that heaven is my home,

00:43:52.540 --> 00:43:55.180
can I tell you what it says in second Corinthians six,

00:43:55.180 --> 00:43:58.580
today is the day of salvation.

00:43:58.580 --> 00:44:00.460
Today is the day of salvation.

00:44:00.460 --> 00:44:04.060
Don't delay, don't leave here without knowing for sure

00:44:04.060 --> 00:44:05.540
that heaven is your home.

00:44:06.480 --> 00:44:09.220
It would thrill my heart, it would thrill our hearts

00:44:09.220 --> 00:44:12.680
for you to trust Christ as your savior today.

00:44:13.700 --> 00:44:15.500
But for a moment, could I speak to the people

00:44:15.500 --> 00:44:16.460
that are saved?

00:44:17.420 --> 00:44:19.100
To those of us that would say,

00:44:19.100 --> 00:44:22.340
hey, I've made that personal decision

00:44:22.340 --> 00:44:24.160
on that particular day.

00:44:24.160 --> 00:44:27.980
I recall just like pastor, you said tomorrow's 29 years.

00:44:27.980 --> 00:44:30.220
I remember X number of years ago

00:44:30.220 --> 00:44:33.800
when I trust that Christ is my savior, I rejoice with you.

00:44:36.300 --> 00:44:38.680
I wonder this morning, are we living for him

00:44:38.680 --> 00:44:40.180
who died for us?

00:44:41.120 --> 00:44:43.260
Second Corinthians chapter five, verse 17,

00:44:43.260 --> 00:44:44.940
I mentioned a few moments ago,

00:44:44.980 --> 00:44:47.280
but verse number 15 says that he died for all

00:44:47.280 --> 00:44:48.980
that they which live should not henceforth

00:44:48.980 --> 00:44:52.180
live unto themselves, but unto him which loved them

00:44:52.180 --> 00:44:53.540
and gave himself for them.

00:44:53.540 --> 00:44:56.380
Listen, this morning we're to live for Jesus.

00:44:56.380 --> 00:44:59.820
We sing the hymn living for Jesus.

00:44:59.820 --> 00:45:02.980
I'm gonna live with him for all of eternity

00:45:02.980 --> 00:45:04.900
if I'm saved, amen.

00:45:04.900 --> 00:45:08.020
If you're saved this morning, you're gonna live with him

00:45:08.020 --> 00:45:09.500
for all of eternity.

00:45:09.500 --> 00:45:14.500
The question really is this, will you live for him today?

00:45:15.420 --> 00:45:17.340
Will you live for him today?

00:45:17.340 --> 00:45:20.860
Will you tell others about Jesus and about his love for them

00:45:20.860 --> 00:45:24.300
and about what he did on Calvary's cross?

00:45:24.300 --> 00:45:26.480
Because the message of salvation is the message

00:45:26.480 --> 00:45:28.540
that the world needs.

00:45:28.540 --> 00:45:30.460
It's a message that's been entrusted to us

00:45:30.460 --> 00:45:33.620
as the people of God to go into all the world

00:45:33.620 --> 00:45:37.060
and preach the gospel to every creature

00:45:37.060 --> 00:45:40.780
because it is absolutely the hope of humanity.

00:45:40.780 --> 00:45:42.900
I was reminded this morning early in my office,

00:45:42.900 --> 00:45:44.200
I don't know if you've seen,

00:45:44.240 --> 00:45:47.180
I've seen some of the footage, horrific footage

00:45:47.180 --> 00:45:50.320
of that flooding situation in Nepal and China.

00:45:50.320 --> 00:45:52.680
Just absolutely blows my mind.

00:45:52.680 --> 00:45:56.480
The devastation, the quickness of all of that happening

00:45:56.480 --> 00:45:58.280
in just a moment.

00:45:58.280 --> 00:46:01.320
And I just wonder this morning if there were maybe some

00:46:01.320 --> 00:46:03.240
that were giving some type of warning

00:46:04.640 --> 00:46:07.120
to get out, to escape.

00:46:07.120 --> 00:46:11.400
You know, the issue is this, that warning can go unheeded.

00:46:11.840 --> 00:46:15.040
There was, it was not raining.

00:46:15.040 --> 00:46:16.960
If you looked at it and understood what happened,

00:46:16.960 --> 00:46:19.880
it wasn't raining and all this kind of thing.

